## Wedding & Event Vendor Marketplace — Cameroon

### 1. YOUR ROLE

Act as a senior full-stack software engineer, UI/UX designer, product manager, database architect, cybersecurity specialist, and startup business strategist.

Your mission is to design, develop, test, and prepare for deployment a modern, responsive, secure, and commercially viable Wedding and Event Vendor Marketplace for Cameroon, launching first in Douala.

Build a functional web application with real navigation, working forms, database integration, authentication, vendor dashboards, search and filtering, and an administration panel. Do not stop at a landing page or static demonstration.

The platform should be scalable to other cities in Cameroon and, eventually, other African countries.

**Working brand:** Ayila'a | Place Sainte Elisa

Treat this as a working brand name. Keep the brand name, logo, contact information, and visual theme configurable so they can be changed later without rebuilding the application.

### 2. BUSINESS OBJECTIVE

Create one trusted online marketplace where individuals, couples, families, businesses, churches, and event planners can discover, compare, contact, and book wedding and event service providers.

The platform should initially serve Douala, Cameroon, and gradually expand to Yaoundé, Buea, Limbe, Bamenda, and other cities.

The platform must solve the following problems:

- Difficulty finding reliable wedding and event vendors.
- Lack of transparent pricing and service packages.
- Difficulty comparing vendors and their portfolios.
- Uncertainty about vendor availability.
- Poor communication between customers and vendors.
- Limited online visibility for small local businesses.
- Difficulty promoting event services to targeted customers.

